  "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#semiotic_projection_1",
  "@type": "SemioticProjection",
  "instance_name": "semiotic_projection_1",
  "label": "User projected onto the collective memory and solemn vow represented by the text and scene",
  "description": "The user is not explicitly projected onto a specific deictic pronoun like 'me' or 'you'. However, the phrase 'we swore we'd never forget' creates an implicit projection where the viewer (user) is positioned as part of the collective 'we' — the group that made the solemn vow to remember the 9/11 attacks. This projection is onto the textual material ('text_chunk_1') and the scene ('burning_twin_towers_scene'), which together evoke a shared, communal identity bound by the trauma and memory of the event. The user is thus projected onto the collective entity of remembrance, symbolized by the burning towers and the vow.",
  "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface",
